  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Bullshit. Objective: Be the first player to get rid of all your cards by playing them to a central pile, either honestly or by bluffing about their rank.',
    Player: 'Bullshit: play by the rules, manage scoring opportunities, and pursue the win condition.',
    objective: 'Be the first player to get rid of all your cards by playing them to a central pile, either honestly or by bluffing about their rank.',
    gameplay: "The game begins with aces (or a chosen rank). The first player plays one or more cards face down, claiming they are aces. Play proceeds clockwise with next rank (2s, then 3s, etc.). After kings, it cycles back to aces. Players can play honestly or bluff. After any play, any other player can challenge by calling 'Bullshit!', 'Cheat!', or 'I Doubt It!'. The played cards are revealed. If the player was lying, they take the entire discard pile. If telling truth, the challenger takes the pile. The winner is first to empty their hand.",
    keyRules: [
      'Cards are played face down to a central pile',
      'Players claim cards are of a specific rank (A, 2, 3...K, then back to A)',
      'Can play 1-4 cards per turn (varies by variant)',
      'Players can bluff (play cards of different rank than claimed)',
      "Any player can challenge a play by calling 'Bullshit!', 'Cheat!', or 'I Doubt It!'",
      'Challenged cards are revealed',
      'If bluffing: player takes the pile',
      'If truthful: challenger takes the pile',
      'Winner is first to empty their hand',
      'Jokers may be wild (can represent any rank)',
